How's that for a fun email title lol

*Brief Note* Sorry for no email last week! I had a lot of things that I did
manage to write, but it wasn=E2=80=99t the whole week, and I didn=E2=80=99t=
 want to send
something that felt incomplete. I have plenty of time to finish things up
though, so it should be a nice long email treat =F0=9F=98=8E

This week we were honored to spend the week in a trio with my 2 Transfer
Earlier Companion, Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81=EF=BC=81As a zone leader he has=
 definitely locked in a
bit more and is really focusing on missionary work. I love this! We were
only able to go housing together once or twice this past week and a little
bit, mostly due to Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 having things to worry about in=
 his area and us
needing to go back and forth lol. It wasn't bad to be busy, but the goal is
definitely still finding more finding time. No reason to be discouraged =F0=
=9F=98=A4
Let's review a few things from this week!

Tuesday we had DCM, and afterwards an exchange =F0=9F=98=8E The sister miss=
ionaries
had to run somewhere after DCM (or we did it online) low key cannot
remember =F0=9F=98=AD=F0=9F=98=82 But we got to eat with the Gobo elders at=
 a fancy crepe place
=F0=9F=98=AE As we were ordering the people in the front gave each of us a =
fancy
latte base in a glass jar for free =F0=9F=A4=B7=E2=80=8D=E2=99=82=EF=B8=8F =
I tried to say I didn't need it
but they said it was a gift so I took it. Now all 5 of us have a little jar
of coffee back at the apartment lol, not sure what we will do with them =F0=
=9F=98=82
Anyways, I got a smoked salmon and avocado crepe with a poached egg and
pesto on top. It was gas, I just wish the toppings were equally spread
across the whole thing, I don't care for presentation as much in that
situation lol. I'll attach a picture if I took one! After eating, we broke
up into our exchange pairs, it was me and Webster=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81, and Do=
wns=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 with my
other 2 comps. Me and Webster=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 stayed behind to get some m=
ore takeout
crepes, while the others left to go back to Sennan. (Crepe shop is in
Wakayama) Although our exchange probably only lasted for 3-5 hours, me and
Webster=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 got to talk about our companions, make plans to c=
ontact
referrals, and have some study time together. It was good to get another
perspective on things =F0=9F=91=8D

This was on either Tuesday or Wednesday, but we also went to go play
volleyball with some people in Wakayama. (Pretty sure tuesday night) It was
super fun. I was only wearing my Proselytizing shoes on the way, so With
around an hour before it started, we went to a thrift store and I bought
the first pair of shoes I picked up without even trying em on. That's real
trust baby. When we got there to play, they fit me to a T. =F0=9F=98=8E Vol=
leyball
was fun, but I was definitely a bit rusty. Having not played much real
volleyball since like 5-6 months ago was rough. Good to get out and do it
though! I had a few good hits. While there we met one of Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=
=80=81=E2=80=99s friends
Ken. He is I think half Japanese, and only recently started living in
Japan. He spent a little bit of his Childhood here but mostly grew up in
America. Super chill guy =F0=9F=98=81 We left Volleyball at probably around=
 10-10:30
and slept over in Wakayama. Way later than we were supposed to be out, if I
realized the time I definitely would have said something I promise =F0=9F=
=99=8F=F0=9F=99=8F=F0=9F=99=8F
We made some good friends so I think it balances out =F0=9F=99=83

The next day (which I think was the exchange) we also had Eikaiwa at the
Sennan church. It was great, and a guy named Shio or something close to
that brought his 7 string guitar to show me. It was beautiful, but it cost
about 4 times as much as the camera I bought in Japan. Yeah so extremely
expensive but it was lit. He's actually insane at the guitar too. He's
played for like 40 years or something. Trying to be like him for real, just
not the cigarettes part =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=85 I want to ask him if we ca=
n practice guitar
together sometime, it might be a good way to connect with him. Mackay=E9=95=
=B7=E8=80=81
kind of spearheaded the Eikaiwa, so it was nice to chill out a bit and be
more of a supporter. It was very fun!

Thursday was my Dad's birthday, so I got to call with him in the morning.
It was nice to have my call with him be right in between P=EF=B8=8Fdays. He=
's
always working hard and showing our family a great spiritual example! I
hope I can strive to go to the temple as often as him when I get the chance=
!

I also found out that one of my 2 working Amps has a button I can press to
play a few different Drum loops, so I can make things sound like a real
rock concert if I want =F0=9F=98=82 Pretty sweet. Later today we got lunch =
again at
Panda Express (Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 was losing his mind over it all wee=
k) and met up
with Romeo and his friend who also showed up! We sat in a semi-circle and
learned Japanese, as well as having a more religious conversation near the
end. We talked more about how important God plays a role in our lives, and
invited Romeo to talk more with us about it when we get the chance. We
learned a bit more of his religious background, turns out he's always been
a member of the Hindu faith back in Nepal, but as he=E2=80=99s been away fr=
om home
and also recovering from a past addiction (pretty sure this was back in
Nepal) hes learned a bit from a teacher with Christian background and
agrees much more with the idea of a merciful and loving God. He said he
didn't yet read from the Book of Mormon, but hopefully soon we can
re-extend that offer to him. He's already agreed to show up to our
Sacrament meeting when his schedule permits, which is amazing. We'll just
have to wait a few weeks and hopefully things will really get moving with
him!

We got to have Eikaiwa in Wakayama, it was pretty fun. We played ping pong
before, and during Eikaiwa I got to sit by and chat with a member most of
the time. Good time!

Today we got to go to a Sakura blossom viewing party with the ward. It was
super pretty, and we also broke into a bunch of groups for different
activities. We played telephone with Hand signs, Arranging ourselves by
birthday without speaking (pretty sure I was the only one out of order =F0=
=9F=98=82)
and had a rick paper scissors tournament, which I decimated. In the first
round I won 15-20 times back to back and the members were losing their
minds. Pur team ended up winning. It was crazy, I think I=E2=80=99ll suck a=
t Rock
paper scissors now for the rest of my life, I accidentally used all of my
powers. Later We got to travel again back to Wakayama and a have a game
night at the church. It was pretty fun but was literally a few rounds of
Uno and another couple card games. Definitely a bit low participation that
day.

We had church, and Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 got to give a brief introductio=
n even though he
wouldn=E2=80=99t even be there next week =F0=9F=98=82 For our Sunday zone d=
evotional we
played a game of Kahoot testing us on the mission standards and I won while
staying in 1st place the whole game =F0=9F=98=8E heck yeah
Today's fruit Basket also insane. Literally more than 10 big bags of
Furugura. I shouldn't have put it on the list of things we want but now I
also have enough to last me 2-3 transfers on my own =F0=9F=98=82

For Pday, we went to Aeon mall With Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and I got some=
 more cards to
fuel my Magic deck for my Companion, as well as some new guitar strings.
Afterwards we went back to the church, and Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and I g=
ot the whole
guitar noce and restrung. It sounds better than ever, and was actually
really fun to learn to restring. The Gobo elders met up with us at the
church and stayed over at our apartment. Crazy fitting 5 people in a 2 man
apartment but It was fun.

Tuesday
Today we had in Person DCM in Sennan, it was fun. We ate as a district at a
Chinese noodle restaurant, which was also pretty cool. I Owed Webster=E9=95=
=B7=E8=80=81
some money from the time we had exchanges and I paid him back 1000=C2=A5 al=
most
entirely in 10yen coins (a few 50 yen coins too) =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82 I=
t was awesome. after
DCM and lunch Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and Me (he=
he) went housing!! It felt
awesome to get out and do some solid Missionary work. I don=E2=80=99t even =
think
anyone had a positive response to our home to home contacting but it felt
so refreshing. Sone housing highlights: Saw the same kid on a bicycle in
like 3 or 4 places, slid down a big pole by some stairs (getting my pants
all dirty), and laughing about random things. The best of times =F0=9F=98=
=89

On Wednesday we visited the okajima family cause we heard that the father
had broken his ankle or hurt it in some other way so he couldn't go to
church for a while. Nobody ended up answering the door, but as we were
sitting in front of the house writing him a note, Sister Okajima pulled up
in her car, so we were able to go inside! Apparently we'd showed up while
Okajima=E5=85=84=E5=BC=9F was in the bath, so we waited a little while and =
he came put to
greet us! With clothes on, of course, weirdo =F0=9F=98=A4 We talked for a w=
hile and
enjoyed some treats including some Yogurt milk, sumo wrestler cookies, and
Japan's equivalent of a creamie. I also recounted my ankle sprain
experience to show a bit of empathy. I suggested we pray together, and
afterwards we left. It was awesome =F0=9F=98=81 As it was Nao's birthday (a=
mazing
woman from Ibaraki (also my Japanese second mother)) I started making some
art for her because it seems like my art is her favorite thing =F0=9F=98=82=
 We played
a bit of ping pong and then we had Eikaiwa. Shiko-san (dude with guitar and
always a pack of cigarettes) brought his main guitar this time, and after
Eikaiwa plugged it into a small Amp he had and blasted some guitar riffs
while members had a meeting in the other room. I told him it was a bit
lound and he proceeded to max out the volume on his Amp saying =E2=80=9Cyou=
 think
this is loud??=E2=80=9D=F0=9F=98=AD=F0=9F=98=AD=F0=9F=98=82 Crazy dude. We'=
ve got plans to meet with him on
Tuesday to practice guitar together! Hopefully it can resonate with him, he
has been coming to Eikaiwa for like 20 years apparently, just not super
interested in Gospel stuff if I had to guess. We will have to find out =F0=
=9F=98=8E

Idk when this was but with Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 we also got to visit a =
members house
for Okonomiyaki (he mentioned he like it during his introduction on Sunday
which prompted a few members to invite him over to eat it =F0=9F=98=82). It=
 was super
delicious, I tried it with Pineapple for the first time. We also shared an
Easter video which had both sweet ladies who made the food in tears, it was
very spiritually strong.

Today I finished my art for Nao, and sent her a video of me playing happy
birthday on the guitar with a message too. She seemed super excited which
is great! Hopefully I will get to see my Ibaraki friends again soon =F0=9F=
=99=8F
Tonight we went out again to eat with Jiro and got some sushi. It was super
good, but even better was the conversation we had with him. He brought up
the word of wisdom, so we talked with him about our beliefs surrounding
what we are allowed to eat and drink. We also talked a bit about temples
and eternal marriage. He seemed to admire our beliefs which is great. Maybe
soon he'll be willing to listen to more of a spiritual thought/lesson type
of thing with us. On the way out of the restaurant I put a few coins in the
Cash machine to help pay for our food, but I didn't notice that Jiro was
already paying with card so I totally jammed the machine, and due to the
place being so shortstaffed it took like 10 minutes for someone to come and
help us =F0=9F=98=82 oopsies

Friday
Today was a low for real. Maybe it was just the lack of momentum from
having Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 leave but we legit didn't leave the apartme=
nt at all. I
think it was a good reminder that things don't just happen on their own. I
got dressed and all ready to go at a =E2=80=9Creasonable time=E2=80=9D but =
never really
encouraged my companion or suggested verbally that we do anything. It's
annoying to feel like I'm making all the decisions and I don't want to be
my comp's mother, but it's also easy to get stuck in that mindset and be
prideful in that way. I think that pride is one of my biggest weaknesses on
the mission I've noticed. I sometimes give my companions or those around me
unrealistic expectations in my own head, and not seek to try and help them
out. By doing so I'm also sinking my actual actions and efforts beneath
what my brain is even saying I'm doing, if that makes any sense. I've gotta
just grit my teeth and say things like =E2=80=9Clet's plan for today,=E2=80=
=9D or =E2=80=9Cwhere
should we go finding?=E2=80=9D It's not hard to do if I'm thinking like the=
 Savior,
bit it's REALLY hard or impossible with a prideful heart. Today was rough
but also gave me a good chance for self reflection. I can be a lot more
humble than I am at times. =F0=9F=98=85=F0=9F=99=8C

Today we did our weekly planning by a stream. Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 dro=
pped his
missionary tag in the water on accident and it started floating away,
luckily he got to it =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82 I took some cool =
pics with my camera, and we
spent time talking about where we wanna go/teach with our friends. On our
bike ride home we ride by a guy taking pictures with his fancy camera, and
I felt like we should stop and go talk with him. I wanted to say something
but it was kind of hard for my companion to hear me from in front on his
bike. Luckily his chapstick fell put of his pocket, so we had to stop and
went back to talk to the Camera guy as well. I'll be darned, he must have
been a ghost or an angel cause when we got back he had vanished. He didn't
exactly have any quick way to escape either, so strange. Next time I need
to be faster to follow a prompting. It was a valuable lesson. Back at the
apartment I was on our Hammock and I fell off and bruised my shoulder and
hip. Still hurting as I write this a few days later =F0=9F=98=82 we had Sus=
hi and
lesson with Suejhiro=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9 and her husband, which was so fun. T=
hey are both so
sweet, and I even got to geek out about some cool Japanese artists I like
with the husband. (go And listen to VAUNDY his music is so dope) We also
had Baskin Robins ice cream back at their house, which was my first time in
Japan. It was pretty good but as i looooce ice cream, those serving were
NOT enough. Just kidding it was enough =F0=9F=98=82

Sunday we didn't go to the church to see General Conference (I didn't know
we had it and Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81=E2=80=99s head apparently hurt when=
 he got up) The weather
was pretty miserable as well, so we didn=E2=80=99t get out of the apartment=
 until
the afternoon. Things cleared up a little bit and so we trekked up to the
church for DCM. We got scolded for being on our phones by one member (even
though I was just taking notes =F0=9F=98=82=EF=BC=89but besides that we hav=
e like 3 new
appointments set up with members to have practice lessons which is awesome.
After DCM, we drove with Brother Otani to the building in which we will
hold another Eikaiwa class starting next month. It should be fun! Sunday
night the Bishop and his wife were sweet enough to invite us over for
dinner again. This time I ate and didn't throw up afterwards, that's a win,
even if it was boring. We taught a little bit about Easter, and watched
some of a video talking about the events leading up to Chirst=E2=80=99s Cru=
cifixion
and resurrection. It was a great experience.

For Pday we went to the mall again (on the way we found a cute little shop
with random anime merchandise), then biked super far to a second street to
look around. I got tricked into buying more playing cards from the mall,
but I actually have enough cards to make a full deck, which is fun but also
means I will likely be more easily convinced to play magic with Magbago=E9=
=95=B7=E8=80=81
which can be a good or a bad thing lol. He could talk about magic all day
long =F0=9F=98=82 (and often does lol) I used a random art idea generator t=
o give me
an idea because I enjoy sharing my art, so heres some art from today!





I am out of time for today, but as this week is leading up to Easter
Sunday, I'd invite anyone reading this to learn more about what the Saviors
Resurrection really means for you. If you don't feel like it even does mean
anything for you, you haven't read or heard enough about it =F0=9F=98=82=F0=
=9F=98=89 I'd
totally challenge you to learn about it and pray about it.

I love you guys! I hope that you are each doing well, I love your emails as
well, I will respond when I can!! Bye!

Killian=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81



