y=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 having things to worry about in his area and us needing=
 to go back and forth lol. It wasn&#39;t bad to be busy, but the goal is de=
finitely still finding more finding time. No reason to be discouraged =F0=
=9F=98=A4 Let&#39;s review a few things from this week!</div><div dir=3D"au=
to"><br></div><div dir=3D"auto">Tuesday we had DCM, and afterwards an excha=
nge =F0=9F=98=8E The sister missionaries had to run somewhere after DCM (or=
 we did it online) low key cannot remember =F0=9F=98=AD=F0=9F=98=82 But we =
got to eat with the Gobo elders at a fancy crepe place =F0=9F=98=AE As we w=
ere ordering the people in the front gave each of us a fancy latte base in =
a glass jar for free =F0=9F=A4=B7=E2=80=8D=E2=99=82=EF=B8=8F I tried to say=
 I didn&#39;t need it but they said it was a gift so I took it. Now all 5 o=
f us have a little jar of coffee back at the apartment lol, not sure what w=
e will do with them =F0=9F=98=82 Anyways, I got a smoked salmon and avocado=
 crepe with a poached egg and pesto on top. It was gas, I just wish the top=
pings were equally spread across the whole thing, I don&#39;t care for pres=
entation as much in that situation lol. I&#39;ll attach a picture if I took=
 one! After eating, we broke up into our exchange pairs, it was me and Webs=
ter=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81, and Downs=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 with my other 2 comps. M=
e and Webster=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 stayed behind to get some more takeout crep=
es, while the others left to go back to Sennan. (Crepe shop is in Wakayama)=
 Although our exchange probably only lasted for 3-5 hours, me and Webster=
=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 got to talk about our companions, make plans to contact =
referrals, and have some study time together. It was good to get another pe=
rspective on things =F0=9F=91=8D</div><div dir=3D"auto"><br></div><div dir=
=3D"auto">This was on either Tuesday or Wednesday, but we also went to go p=
lay volleyball with some people in Wakayama. (Pretty sure tuesday night) It=
 was super fun. I was only wearing my Proselytizing shoes on the way, so Wi=
th around an hour before it started, we went to a thrift store and I bought=
 the first pair of shoes I picked up without even trying em on. That&#39;s =
real trust baby. When we got there to play, they fit me to a T. =F0=9F=98=
=8E Volleyball was fun, but I was definitely a bit rusty. Having not played=
 much real volleyball since like 5-6 months ago was rough. Good to get out =
and do it though! I had a few good hits. While there we met one of Mackay=
=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81=E2=80=99s friends Ken. He is I think half Japanese, and =
only recently started living in Japan. He spent a little bit of his Childho=
od here but mostly grew up in America. Super chill guy =F0=9F=98=81 We left=
 Volleyball at probably around 10-10:30 and slept over in Wakayama. Way lat=
er than we were supposed to be out, if I realized the time I definitely wou=
ld have said something I promise =F0=9F=99=8F=F0=9F=99=8F=F0=9F=99=8F We ma=
de some good friends so I think it balances out =F0=9F=99=83</div><div dir=
=3D"auto"><br></div><div dir=3D"auto">The next day (which I think was the e=
xchange) we also had Eikaiwa at the Sennan church. It was great, and a guy =
named Shio or something close to that brought his 7 string guitar to show m=
e. It was beautiful, but it cost about 4 times as much as the camera I boug=
ht in Japan. Yeah so extremely expensive but it was lit. He&#39;s actually =
insane at the guitar too. He&#39;s played for like 40 years or something. T=
rying to be like him for real, just not the cigarettes part =F0=9F=98=82=F0=
=9F=98=85 I want to ask him if we can practice guitar together sometime, it=
 might be a good way to connect with him. Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 kind of =
spearheaded the Eikaiwa, so it was nice to chill out a bit and be more of a=
 supporter. It was very fun!</div><div dir=3D"auto"><br></div><div dir=3D"a=
uto">Thursday was my Dad&#39;s birthday, so I got to call with him in the m=
orning. It was nice to have my call with him be right in between P=EF=B8=8F=
days. He&#39;s always working hard and showing our family a great spiritual=
 example! I hope I can strive to go to the temple as often as him when I ge=
t the chance!</div><div dir=3D"auto"><br></div><div dir=3D"auto">I also fou=
nd out that one of my 2 working Amps has a button I can press to play a few=
 different Drum loops, so I can make things sound like a real rock concert =
